<VI _name="lvai_set_representation.vi" description="Changes the REPRESENTATION of numerics of an existing VI or .ctl IN PLACE\2C then saves the file\3A front-panel controls and indicators (cluster elements and the fields of a typedef included\2C at any depth) and block diagram constants\2C each found by its LABEL.\0A\0AMEASURED 2026-11-20 on LabVIEW 2026\3A the Representation property of {LV.Numeric} and of {LV.NumericConstant} is WRITABLE in edit mode\2C although the catalogue lists it as read. It is an enum of uint32\3A 0 EXT\2C 1 DBL\2C 2 SGL\2C 3 I32\2C 4 I16\2C 5 I8\2C 6 U32\2C 7 U16\2C 8 U8\2C 9..11 complex\2C 12 I64\2C 13 U64\2C 14 fixed-point. The value and the default survive\2C the wires stay\2C and a sink of the old type gets a coercion dot. A typedef field is written the same way on the .ctl itself\3B the callers follow when they are next loaded and are saved by the caller of this helper.\0A\0AA NUMBER OUT OF RANGE IS NOT REFUSED BY LABVIEW. Writing 99 answered no error and left the control FIXED-POINT with its default gone. The caller sends only the numbers above.\0A\0AWHY TRAVERSE. Traverse for GObjects with class name Numeric returns every numeric of the panel at any depth\2C the elements of a cluster included\2C so a typedef's field is reached without walking Controls[]. On the diagram the class name is NumericConstant.\0A\0AA LABEL MUST MATCH EXACTLY ONE OBJECT. matches reports\2C per requested label and in request order\2C how many numerics carried it\3B only a label with exactly one match is written\2C the shape lvai_swap_subvis uses for constants. The references and labels are collected ONCE before any write.\0A\0AONE ERROR CHAIN\2C SO THE FILE IS ALL OR NOTHING. A write LabVIEW refuses - an enum asked to become a float is error 1077 - leaves its error on the wire\2C the writes after it do not run and Save.Instrument does not save. codes names\2C per request\2C the error at that point of the chain\3A the first nonzero entry is the request that failed. after is the representation read back in the session\2C -1 where nothing was written.\0A\0ATWO RUNS. With save FALSE and no labels the helper only LISTS\3A control labels seen and constant labels seen name every numeric there is\2C and nothing is written - an unchanged file is never re-saved in the running LabVIEW's version for nothing. With no labels and save TRUE it loads and saves the file\2C which is how a typedef's caller is brought up to date. The diagram traverse's own error does not reach the save\3A a .ctl has no block diagram\2C and then no constant is found.\0A\0AThe VI is opened in the instance this helper runs in\2C or\2C with through active project TRUE\2C in the active project's application instance\3A both were measured to save the same file. Lists are pipe separated\2C the way lvai_swap_subvis passes them.">
